ralph/progress.txt:32087:  - The repository surface for project_grants is intentionally narrow (Upsert + ListByProject + DeleteByProjectExceptIDs); there is NO per-id Get, no per-id Delete, no traditional Update. Tests must adapt: the rollback proof reduces to a ListByProject probe (the only observation surface) and the duplicate-id test must use a different principal_id so the ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match and the PRIMARY KEY (id) violation is exercised instead.
ralph/progress.txt:32090:  - The `seedProjectGrant` raw-SQL helper in project_grant_test.go (sibling file, same store_test package) is deliberately complementary, NOT a duplicate of `upsertProjectGrant` here. project_grant_test.go's tests exercise the READ path against schema-inserted rows; this file exercises the repository's INSERT path. A regression in repo.Upsert would still let the sibling read tests pass — exactly the kind of seam this file is designed to catch.
ralph/progress.txt:32141:  - Test name collisions check: `grep '^func Test' internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_test.go internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_repository_invariants_test.go` BEFORE adding new test names. project_grant_test.go uses TestProjectGrantRepo* and TestProjectGrantReader* (the read-only path), project_grant_repository_invariants_test.go uses TestProjectGrantRepository* (the CRUD path); this file extends the TestProjectGrantRepository* family with unique suffixes (...OnOrgADoesNotTouchOrgB, ...CrossTenantProjectIDReturnsEmpty, ...IsolatesSharedPrincipal, ...InTwoTenantsBothSucceed). The BE-0429 store_test package collision rule applies — every new test in store_test must be globally unique.
ralph/progress.txt:32147:- Added internal/controlplane/store/environment_repository_invariants_test.go (6 integration tests + 2 file-scope helpers) covering EnvironmentRepository's CRUD row-shape and lifecycle invariants. The environments table has a SMALLER mutation surface than projects (Insert + Update + ScheduleDeletion only; NO UpdateDisplayName, NO Restore), so the invariants matrix is correspondingly smaller than project_repository_invariants_test.go's.
