ralph/progress.txt:32257:  - The services table is the FIRST table in the priority order whose mutation surface is BOTH Insert + Update + ScheduleDeletion AND Restore (environments stopped at ScheduleDeletion; projects has all four — services mirrors projects's lifecycle shape). The invariants matrix therefore replicates project_repository_invariants_test.go's structure — Insert version/timestamp / Update dual-anchor / Update If-Match / ScheduleDeletion dual-anchor / Restore dual-anchor / Insert tx rollback / nil-Tx guards — adapted to the services row's extra columns. Future tables that share this lifecycle (any tenant-scoped resource with soft-delete + restore) should reuse the same template.
ralph/progress.txt:32258:  - Services has TWO load-bearing immutability properties Update must protect that projects/environments do NOT: (1) the composite (organization_id, project_id, environment_id) tenant key — three columns, not two — must be byte-preserved, since a re-parenting through Update would silently move the service to another environment with no audit trail; (2) Kind is immutable Dokploy taxonomy (the kind CHECK in migration 0002 enforces the {"application","database","compose"} closed set, but the CHECK does not prevent moving WITHIN that set). The Update test deliberately seeds desired.Kind = testutil.ServiceKindDatabase against a baseline application row to prove the repository's SQL `SET slug = $3, display_name = $4` clause does not include kind and the persisted row keeps the baseline kind verbatim.
ralph/progress.txt:32260:  - Helper naming check: `grep '^func ' internal/controlplane/store/*_test.go` BEFORE adding helpers. `seedService` is taken by schema_test.go (raw-SQL fixture seeder returning testutil.Service); the invariants file's `insertService` is intentionally distinct in BOTH name and return type (it returns store.Service after going through repo.Insert + Store.Write, exercising the production code path). `serviceFixture` mirrors `environmentFixture` / `projectFixture` — a pure data transform with no DB access, lifting testutil.Service into the store.Service shape the repository accepts.
ralph/progress.txt:32261:  - The typed rollback sentinel must have a globally-unique struct name across the store_test package since every *_test.go file shares the same package. Naming convention: `<resource>TxRollbackSentinel` (e.g. serviceTxRollbackSentinel here, projectTxRollbackSentinel in project_repository_invariants_test.go). The header doc on the sentinel type cross-references the other six sentinels to make the collision rule explicit for future stories.
ralph/progress.txt:32262:  - Codebase Patterns: NOT adding a new top-level entry here. The pattern is a direct mirror of project_repository_invariants_test.go (the "Repository-layer CRUD-and-lifecycle invariants test file for a tenant-scoped resource with soft-delete + restore" pattern is already documented under BE-0407 / projects). The two services-specific deltas (three-column composite tenant key, immutable Dokploy taxonomy kind) are story-specific learnings here; if a future table lands with the same shape (services-like lifecycle + canonical-kind CHECK + composite parent FK), promote them then.
ralph/progress.txt:32266:- Added internal/controlplane/store/service_tenant_isolation_test.go modeled on environment_tenant_isolation_test.go (BE-0442). Proves the services table is tenant-scoped at every repository surface via byte-identical bystander assertions on (id, organization_id, project_id, environment_id, slug, display_name, kind, version, created_at, updated_at, deletion_scheduled_at). Thirteen test cases covering: GetByID correct row per tenant, GetByID cross-tenant indistinguishable from unknown id (Code + Hint identity), ListByEnvironment count isolation, ListByEnvironment shared-slug isolation, ListByEnvironment cross-tenant/unknown empty-slice symmetry, Update bystander byte-identical (own-tenant write + cross-tenant NotFound), ScheduleDeletion bystander byte-identical (both directions), Restore bystander byte-identical against BOTH a live peer (nil stamp) and a soft-deleted peer (non-nil stamp), Insert shared-slug-in-two-tenants both-succeed (UNIQUE (environment_id, slug) per-environment), and soft-deleted row tenant-scoped across GetByID + ListByEnvironment with owner still seeing own soft-deleted row.
ralph/progress.txt:32281:  - The services repository surface differs from environments: services has Restore as a sibling to ScheduleDeletion (environments does not). Restore tests use Insert(v1) → ScheduleDeletion(v2) → Restore(v3) for the version-bump assertion.
ralph/progress.txt:32291:- Added internal/controlplane/store/service_grant_repository_invariants_test.go: 13 t.Parallel tests covering Upsert insert (timestamps byte-equal on fresh row, version=1, fields echoed verbatim), Upsert insert with service-account principal kind, Upsert update branch (only role mutates; caller id ignored; cross-kind smuggling impossible; version bumped; updated_at refreshed; created_at preserved), cross-tenant FK rejected as typed Conflict, unknown service_id rejected as typed Conflict, duplicate PK rejected as typed Conflict, DeleteByServiceExceptIDs nil-keep clears all, DeleteByServiceExceptIDs non-empty-keep removes only excluded, DeleteByServiceExceptIDs tenant-scoped (cross-tenant predicate matches zero rows), ON DELETE CASCADE from services, Upsert tx-rollback (observed through ListByService — the only read surface), and Upsert + DeleteByServiceExceptIDs nil-Tx guards as typed Internal.
