ralph/progress.txt:32610:- Implemented: internal/controlplane/store/quota_policy_repository_invariants_test.go — repository-level invariants for QuotaRepository's quota_policies write surface (UpsertOrganizationPolicy) and the ListEffectiveLimits resolver. The existing quota_repository_test.go already owned the per-resource EffectiveLimit semantics (PrefersOrgOverride / FallsBackToPlanDefault / NotFound / TenantScoped) and the reservation flows, so this file is additive only — it pins what the existing file does NOT: INSERT row shape (qpol_<token> id, scope_kind='organization', plan IS NULL, organization_id, timestamps), UPDATE branch identity preservation (id and created_at byte-equal, updated_at refreshed), plan-default rows untouched by org override upserts, FK violation -> Conflict on unknown organization_id, negative limit -> Conflict, unknown enforcement_mode -> Conflict, every EnforcementMode constant round-trips, ListEffectiveLimits deterministic alpha order with override-beats-default, ListEffectiveLimits tenant scoping (orgB cannot see orgA's overrides), ListEffectiveLimits plan isolation (a 'pro' default does not bleed into a 'starter' read), ListEffectiveLimits empty result when unconfigured, Store.Write closure rollback proven via a typed sentinel (errors.Is + EffectiveLimit reports unconfigured), and nil-tx guard -> yerr.CodeInternal.
