ralph/progress.txt:32808:  - The `quota_reservations` table is the third member of the quota_* family but its public repository surface is the SMALLEST of the three: InsertReservation (active-row mint, no upsert) + SumActiveReservations (predicate-filtered sum). There is NO per-row Get / Update / Commit / Release / Expire on the repository yet -- the lifecycle landings happen in the worker-side provisioning-jobs PRD. The invariants file MUST acknowledge this in its file-doc comment so a future reader does not look for a missing Commit/Release test.
ralph/progress.txt:32809:  - Migration 0008 added a composite FK `quota_reservations_job_fk` from `quota_reservations (organization_id, job_id)` to `provisioning_jobs (organization_id, id)`. The repository's `InsertReservation` does NOT pre-validate that the job exists -- it relies on the FK -- so a test that round-trips a non-empty `JobID` MUST pre-seed a real `provisioning_jobs` row (minimum required columns: `id`, `organization_id`, `job_type`, `idempotency_key`; every other column has a default) before calling `InsertReservation`. The seed can be a raw `db.Exec` -- there is no `seedProvisioningJob` test helper yet.
ralph/progress.txt:32811:  - `InsertReservation` can only mint ACTIVE rows by construction: its INSERT column list omits `settled_at`, so passing a non-blank, non-'active' `Status` produces an inconsistent (status<>'active' AND settled_at IS NULL) row that the `quota_reservations_settled_consistent` CHECK rejects. This is the canonical invariant for the repository's settled-state contract -- a future Commit/Release/Expire repository method that DOES write `settled_at` will need its OWN settled-state invariants test.
ralph/progress.txt:32814:  - The full `go test ./internal/controlplane/store/` run is currently flaky under parallel-DB pressure due to Postgres connection-pool / database-creation rate limits (the `service_quota_*_concurrent_test.go` family creates many isolated databases and runs many parallel goroutines, occasionally hitting `E_UNAVAILABLE`). The flake reproduces at HEAD without this change. For verifying a single repository invariants story, run `go test -run '<TestFamily>' ./internal/controlplane/store/` in isolation; the full-package run is best left to CI with serialised concurrency.
