ralph/progress.txt:32929:  - **Append-only repositories in this codebase carry NO updated_at column, NO version column, AND a BEFORE UPDATE trigger.** All three are load-bearing: omitting updated_at + version means peer-row byte-identity tests are simpler (only id + content columns can drift, and the trigger forbids drift); adding the trigger means the immutability holds even when an operator bypasses the repository surface with raw SQL through a console. The pattern is shared with audit_events; deployment_events extends it with a composite FK to a deeper parent (deployments) so the cascade chain runs through two ON DELETE CASCADE legs (deployments -> events, then organizations -> deployments -> events on tenant teardown).
ralph/progress.txt:32930:  - **The application-boundary error class for "the application caught this before the database had a chance" is apierr.Internal, not apierr.InvalidInput.** A blank EventType at the repository's Append surface is a programming error (the application should never send it; the closed set is a Go type) — the typed code is yerr.CodeInternal. apierr.InvalidInput is reserved for the HTTP/service layer where the customer's request is being validated; a repository call site has no customer-facing context. Same pattern as AuditRepository.Append rejecting an invalid Decision with Internal.
