ralph/progress.txt:33357:  - There is NO updated_at column on job_attempts (unlike provisioning_jobs / deployments / projects / services), so the trigger-managed-anchor invariant used in deployment_tenant_isolation_test.go's assertDeploymentByteIdentical and job_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go's assertJobByteIdentical does NOT apply here. assertJobAttemptByteIdentical compares created_at as the sole timestamp anchor (alongside started_at + finished_at as caller-supplied anchors that should remain caller-supplied verbatim under any well-formed regression). The pattern note for future append-only tables: if the table has no updated_at AND the BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejects all updates, the byte-identity bystander proof is mostly probing the trigger AND the predicate -- a regression that silently dropped the trigger would surface as a column rewrite the per-field assertJobAttemptByteIdentical catches.
