+  - `staticcheck ./...` was not run because `staticcheck` is not installed.
+  - `govulncheck ./...` was not run because `govulncheck` is not installed.
+- Results
+  - Required formatting, module, test, race, and vet gates passed.
+  - Optional `golangci-lint` passed with `0 issues`.
+  - The repository conventions static test passed after the guide and release-gate wiring were added.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups
+  - No live Dokploy smoke was run; this documentation story does not require one and the smoke remains opt-in.
+  - Install `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` locally to exercise the optional gates outside CI.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Development documentation stories should add a static release test first, then wire the document into `scripts/verify.sh`, CI, SECURITY.md, and `internal/release/AGENTS.md`.
+  - Static doc tests intentionally match exact operator-facing phrases, so keep key acceptance-criteria sentences stable and unwrapped when the tests assert them literally.
+---
